    "term": "ELT",
    "fullName": "Emergency locator transmitter",
    "description": "Emergency Locator Transmitter (ELT) is a battery-powered emergency radio beacon installed on aircraft that, upon impact or manual activation, transmits a distress signal to facilitate Search and Rescue (SAR) operations. Modern 406 MHz ELTs transmit coded digital signals including the aircraft's registration and GPS position to COSPAS-SARSAT satellites, dramatically reducing false alarm rates and enabling near-instant position determination. Aircraft must also carry the older 121.5 MHz signal for backward compatibility with aircraft searching for the signal.",
