    "term": "RVSM",
    "description": "Reduced Vertical Separation Minima (RVSM) is an airspace standard that reduces the vertical separation between aircraft from 2,000 feet to 1,000 feet in the flight level band FL290–FL410. RVSM effectively doubles the number of usable flight levels in this heavily trafficked altitude range, significantly increasing airspace capacity. RVSM approval requires aircraft with certified accurate altimetry systems (two independent altimeters, automatic altitude control, and altitude alerter), crew training, and regulatory authorization.",
    "category": "NOTAM",
