    "term": "DME",
    "fullName": "Distance measuring equipment",
    "description": "Distance Measuring Equipment (DME) is a radio navigation system enabling aircraft to determine their slant-range distance from a ground station by measuring the time delay of UHF pulse pairs (interrogations) transmitted by the aircraft and answered by the ground transponder. DME operates in the 960–1215 MHz band and is typically co-located with VOR or ILS to provide complete bearing and distance information. DME/DME RNAV uses two or more DME stations geometrically to compute precise position fixes.",
