    "term": "GPS",
    "fullName": "Global positioning system",
    "description": "Global Positioning System (GPS) is a U.S.-operated satellite navigation system providing precise position, velocity, and time information to suitably equipped aircraft. Aviation GPS receivers use signals from at least four satellites to compute three-dimensional position with accuracy typically better than 10 meters. GPS supports all phases of flight including oceanic, en-route, terminal, and approach operations. Wide Area Augmentation System (WAAS) and Ground Based Augmentation System (GBAS) provide the enhanced accuracy and integrity needed for precision GPS approaches (LPV).",
