    "term": "SIGMET",
    "description": "Significant Meteorological Information (SIGMET) is an official weather advisory issued by a Meteorological Watch Office (MWO) to warn aircraft operators of potentially hazardous weather phenomena en route, not already included in forecasts. SIGMETs cover thunderstorms (OBSC, EMBD, FRQ, SQL TS), severe turbulence, severe icing, mountain waves, tropical cyclones, volcanic ash, and radioactive material clouds. SIGMETs are coded in international meteorological format and broadcast on HF radio and via ACARS/AFTN. Non-convective SIGMETs are valid up to 4 hours, convective SIGMETs up to 2 hours.",
    "category": "PilotController",
