    "term": "VFR",
    "fullName": "Visual flight rules",
    "description": "Visual Flight Rules (VFR) are a set of aviation regulations under which a pilot operates an aircraft by visual reference to the ground or other landmarks, without necessarily relying on aircraft instruments. VFR flight requires minimum visibility (typically 5 km at or above 3,000 ft AMSL, 1,500 m below) and minimum distance from clouds. VFR flights do not inherently require ATC clearances in uncontrolled airspace but must comply with all airspace requirements. VFR flight plans are recommended for cross-country navigation.",
