    "term": "VOR",
    "fullName": "VHF omnidirectional radio range",
    "description": "VHF Omnidirectional Range (VOR) is a type of short-range radio navigation system enabling aircraft to determine their position and track to or from the station. VORs operate in the frequency range 108–117.95 MHz and transmit two signals: a reference phase and a variable phase whose relationship changes with direction. The onboard VOR receiver compares the two signals to determine the aircraft's radial (magnetic bearing) from the station. VORs are combined with DME as VOR/DME or VORTAC (VOR/TACAN) to provide both bearing and distance.",
    "category": "PilotController",
