    "term": "BRAKING ACTION",
    "fullName": "Braking Action",
    "description": "Braking Action is the standardized qualitative description used by pilots to report the effectiveness of aircraft braking, directional control, and deceleration on a runway surface. Under the ICAO Global Reporting Format (GRF) and FAA TALPA framework, braking action is reported using six standardized terms: Good (RWYCC 5  normal deceleration, normal directional control), Good to Medium (RWYCC 4), Medium (RWYCC 3  noticeably reduced deceleration and directional control), Medium to Poor (RWYCC 2), Poor (RWYCC 1  significantly reduced deceleration and directional control), and Less than Poor/Nil (RWYCC 0  minimal to non-existent deceleration, uncertain directional control). Braking action reports are submitted by flight crews immediately after landing or rejected takeoff, and are used by aerodrome operators to validate or downgrade the published RWYCC via the RCAM Downgrade Assessment Criteria. The reporting system replaced the old Good/Fair/Poor scale with a more precise six-level scale directly correlated with aircraft performance data.",
