    "term": "TAWS",
    "fullName": "Terrain Awareness and Warning System",
    "description": "Terrain Awareness and Warning System (TAWS) is an avionics system that provides terrain conflict warnings to flight crews. Class A TAWS (equivalent to EGPWS) incorporates a digital terrain database with forward-looking terrain avoidance (FLTA), premature descent alert (PDA), and basic GPWS functions. Class B TAWS provides reduced functionality including FLTA and PDA but without some GPWS modes, and is typically installed in smaller aircraft. Class C TAWS is a hybrid system combining the display and database features with basic GPWS. TAWS uses GPS position and aircraft performance data to predict potential terrain conflicts and provides both aural and visual warnings with sufficient time for evasive action (typically 30-60 seconds before impact). The system is mandated by 14 CFR Part 91.223 for turbine-powered aircraft with 6+ passenger seats and by Part 135.153 for certain aircraft operations. TAWS terrain databases are updated periodically to reflect changes in obstacles and airport infrastructure.",
