    "term": "RNP AR",
    "fullName": "Required Navigation Performance Authorization Required",
    "description": "Required Navigation Performance Authorization Required (RNP AR) is a specialized category of RNP approach procedure requiring specific aircraft certification, crew training, and operational approval from the aviation authority. RNP AR approaches are characterized by very tight navigation tolerances (typically RNP 0.1 to 0.3 NM) and are designed to provide access to airports in challenging terrain or with limited infrastructure. Key requirements for RNP AR operations include: (a) aircraft must have dual FMS with fault detection and exclusion (FDE) capability; (b) crew must complete specific RNP AR training including simulator sessions; (c) the operator must receive operational authorization from the regulatory authority; (d) special contingency procedures for loss of RNP capability in the terminal area; (e) approach-specific NOTAM monitoring for ground-based navigation aid outages; and (f) barometric altimeter temperature compensation when required. RNP AR approaches typically provide curved approach paths, multiple step-down fixes, and lower minima than conventional approaches, significantly improving access to terrain-challenged airports.",
