    "term": "OCA",
    "fullName": "Obstacle Clearance Altitude",
    "description": "Obstacle Clearance Altitude (OCA) is the lowest altitude above the elevation of the relevant runway threshold or above the aerodrome elevation used in establishing compliance with appropriate obstacle clearance criteria for an instrument approach procedure. OCA is determined by calculating the required clearance above all obstacles in the approach area, considering aircraft category and approach type. For precision approaches, OCA is equivalent to the Decision Altitude (DA); for non-precision approaches, OCA is equivalent to the Minimum Descent Altitude (MDA). OCA is calculated by the procedure designer and published on approach charts. The obstacle clearance provided varies by approach segment: initial approach (1000 ft in non-mountainous, 2000 ft in mountainous), intermediate (500 ft), final (typically 250 ft for precision, 250-300 ft for non-precision), and missed approach (50 ft for each 1 NM from threshold for precision, 100 ft for non-precision).",
